## Join Or Create Room

Quick match: enters a visible open room with a free seat, the same `maxPlayers` and exactly the same `filter`, or creates a visible room when none fits. Returns the room code.

| Option             | Type              | Description                                                                                                                          |
| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `maxPlayers`       | number            | Players meet only in rooms of the same size.                                                                                         |
| `filter`           | flat object       | Matchmaking key, up to 16 values: players meet only in rooms with exactly the same filter. No filter matches only rooms without one. |
| `properties`       | flat object       | Extra properties of a created room.                                                                                                  |
| `playerProperties` | flat object       | As in [Create Room](#create-room).                                                                                                   |
| `syncState`        | boolean or object | As in [Create Room](#create-room).                                                                                                   |

Put the game version or mode into `filter` so that incompatible builds never meet.

Keep the filter to the splits that really matter: every extra key and value divides the players into smaller pools, and with few players online at once each one ends up alone in its own room. Never put unique values into it (a match or invite code, a player or QA id, a build hash, a timestamp): no other player has the same filter, so nobody ever joins. Values that only describe the match (map, league, skin, round) go into `properties`.

If the game mechanics allow it, keep the room open while the match is running, for example with bots filling the empty seats, instead of closing it with `setRoomOpen(false)` right away: then a player who starts the quick match a bit later joins this room and does not create a new one.

