## Regions

Optional. By default the server picks the best region for the player, so most games do not need this. Use it to let the player choose a region themselves.

`getRegions()` returns the ids of the server regions, for example `['eu', 'us', 'ap']`, for a region picker. `region` is the region of the next room created with `createRoom()` or `joinOrCreateRoom()` and of `getRooms()`; it is empty until `getRegions()`, `setRegion()` or the first room call, and `getRegions()` sets it to the region the server picks for the player. `setRegion(id)` changes it; the room the player is in stays where it is. `joinRoom()` with a room code always enters the region of the room, whatever region is selected.

The choice lasts while the page is open. To keep it between launches, save it in [storage](https://wiki.playgama.com/playgama/bridge-sdk/api/storage.md) and call `setRegion()` on start.

